      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three or four times daily** (2,400\u20133,200 mg/day, the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing)\n- **1600 mg/day divided** in some other way\n- **1600 mg four times daily** exactly as written. If so, please confirm, and I'll enter it with a note saying the dose was verified by the attending.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
     ],
